  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2020-08-08T14:40:16.913Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Hello, I seem to have encountered a problem that might not be the easiest to spot due to every avatar being different. There seems to be a problem with the upper arms twisting due to some sort of IK function, this was not present before avatars 3.0 got a full release. The easiest method to test this is to get an SDK2 avatar on desktop mode and crouch, you should notice that the upper arms are twisting backwards (the direction away from the body). Since this is so visible on my own avatar I also noticed that this happens to my 3.0 version as well, except it's much worse. The arms are twisted like that all the time no matter what with the new system unless I play an animation emote. The twisted arms disappear for the duration of the avatar performing the animation, as soon as it goes back to it's original state the arms twist again. I tried redoing my avatar for 3.0 several times with the exact same results. All of the proper steps were followed for setting up a basic avatar. I have included an image of the issue on my avatar.",
